This product implements mechanisms described in C. S. Wright, "On Immutable
Memory Systems for Artificial Agents" (arXiv:2506.13246). Patent and licence
observations are in docs/v2-legal-notes.md and docs/RESEARCH.md; they are
technical notes, not legal advice, and this licence grants no rights in
third-party patents.

Proof sharding (selective proof of existence, DIS-002): this product
implements a mechanism claimed by nChain's US 12,730,827 B2 patent (granted
2026-09-08) under the Open BSV pledge — nChain/BSVA's grant of free use of
its patent portfolio on BSV (including its testnets), revocable for
non-BSV use. nektar is BSV-only by construction. Operators who do not rely
on the pledge can disable the feature entirely with
NEKTAR_PROOF_SHARDING=0 (the proveSubset/verifySubset tools then return
'disabled').

Third-party components are listed in sbom.cdx.json (CycloneDX) with their
own licences. Test vectors in vectors/smt-rust.json and vectors/curve-rust.json
were generated by running third-party Rust crates (identity-attribution
idattr-smt, triple-entry-evidence-bsv bsvcurve) as oracles.
